      "writtenOn": "2022-03-28T20:54:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think I was unclear in my previous comment about the format of this state. In theory, the partner emulators will eventually need to handle most possible incoming message types to cover the entire TCPM. However, PD only ever has one atomic message sequence going at a time. If an unexpected message comes in during an AMS, either it\u0027s a protocol error (uninterruptible AMS), or it cancels the previous AMS (interruptible AMS). So there\u0027s no particular reason that this needs to be a bit field, and I would suggest just making it an `enum pd_ctrl_msg_type` and using 0 to represent no active AMS.",
      "revId": "e9f9bb1db3f23b8adb45982d56acb0862c20ffe3",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
