      "writtenOn": "2022-03-28T20:54:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yuval: I think this concept is original to this emulator. At least, I\u0027m unfamiliar.\n\nAl: The implementations of these functions make clear that only one control message type may be active at a time. If this is the case, then I don\u0027t think the caller needs to be aware that the underlying data structure used by this function is a mask. The function can just be called something like set_active_control_message. See my other comment about whether it makes sense to use a mask for this.",
